SWEET AMP VI TX (patch 0179, plan A10g), on top of 0178: boot-arg sweetaoc=13. Run a10f (0178) found zeros in every ASPRX1 slot 0..7 at
ASP width 32 and 16 on both amps while the AOC consumed the tone: the TDM0 data line carries no PCM although BCLK/FSYNC run (PLL locked).
The one stock speaker-playback difference left on the amp side: the VI feedback the amps transmit on TDM_0_TX (stock mixer defaults ASP TX1
VMON / TX2 IMON, slots L 0/2, R 1/3; HAL path "hostless-ulC spk-vi"). This level turns ASPTX1/2 on with those slots, plays a 12 s
continuous tone with the 0177 ASPRX1 detector and meters every 2 s, then turns TX off and restores. Levels <= 12 unchanged.

